---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
---
<Shell title="Brand studio · review"><div class="wrap"><div class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Brand studio · direction 01</p><h1>Earth, sea<br/>and a shared story.</h1><p class="lead">The book opens. The boat travels. A warm, bilingual identity for the knowledge we carry forward.</p></div><p class="notice">For Founder review. Name, tagline and colour families are agreed. The refined symbol, type pairing and illustration below are proposals.</p>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:15px"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 · The identity</p><h2>One idea. Three ways to say it.</h2></div></div><div class="brand-grid"><div><div class="lockup"><Brand/></div><p class="option-note"><strong>A · Bilingual literary — recommended</strong>Noto Serif Odia with an English serif. A warm, recognisable masthead that keeps both scripts together.</p></div><div><div class="lockup"><Brand variant="bilingual sans"/></div><p class="option-note"><strong>B · Bilingual contemporary</strong>Noto Sans Odia with the same English serif. A quieter, more contemporary reading of the identity.</p></div><div><div class="lockup"><Brand variant="english"/></div><p class="option-note"><strong>C · English compact</strong>Useful at small sizes and for international contexts. Odia remains present elsewhere in the experience.</p></div></div><div class="screen-proof"><div><p class="eyebrow">24 px symbol test</p><img class="small-mark" src="/assets/book-boat-v1.png" alt="Small book-and-boat symbol"/></div><div class="proof-dark"><Brand variant="english"/></div><div><p style="font-size:12px;max-width:290px">The current symbol is a raster concept. A final vector master and optical adjustments at small sizes follow logo selection.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">02 · The material palette</p><h2>Mankada leads. The others support.</h2><div class="palette"><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--earth)"><span lang="or">ମାଙ୍କଡ଼ା ପଥର</span><div>Mankada Pathara<br/><small>#91462F · Primary identity, headings, key actions</small></div></div><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--sea)"><span lang="or">ନୀଳ ସାଗର</span><div>Nila Sagara<br/><small>#1D4658 · Links, depth, supporting contrast</small></div></div><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--olive)"><span lang="or">ଶୁଖା ଘଷି</span><div>Sukha Ghasi<br/><small>#74633B · Olive / #C1A263 · Straw</small></div></div></div><p style="font-size:13px;margin-top:18px;color:var(--muted)">Warm paper #F2E6D0 and reading ink #302E28 complete the palette. These are working digital interpretations of the Founder’s material references.</p></section>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">03 · The visual world</p><h2>A little ornament. Space to read.</h2><figure class="art-review"><img src="/assets/coast-illustration-v1.png" alt="Proposed coastal illustration with a boat, foliage and patterned water." loading="lazy"/><figcaption>New AI-assisted concept illustration based on the preferred earlier board. It evokes a coast; it does not document a real place or historic voyage. Documentary photographs will be credited separately.</figcaption></figure><div class="brand-decisions"><h3>The decisions to make</h3><ol><li>Choose the default lockup: A, B or C.</li><li>Confirm the refined book-and-boat symbol, or identify what to adjust.</li><li>Confirm this balance of illustration and quiet reading space on the homepage.</li></ol><p style="font-size:13px;margin-top:18px">Suggested first direction: A, the book-and-boat symbol, and one illustration-led homepage. Use simpler typography-led article pages for sustained reading.</p></div></section><section class="prose section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">04 · The story we keep</p><h2>Colours with a memory.</h2><p>The palette began with your references to stone, sea, dry straw and muted olive. You connected Sukha Ghasi with cow dung and paddy straw used as cooking fuel, then made Mankada Pathara the dominant colour. These are your supplied associations; we have not invented a childhood scene or a historical origin for them.</p><p>The earlier board, the naming corrections and the discussion are preserved in the project’s history. The word <span lang="or" style="font-family:OdiaSerif">ଉତ୍କଳ</span> is live Odia text, rendered with the included Noto fonts. The approved project name remains <strong>Utkal Project</strong>.</p><p style="font-size:12px">Design direction: Ahimanikya Satapathy. Design and image-generation assistance: AI. Noto fonts retain their included open font licences. This preview is not a final logo approval.</p><a href="/" class="button">See it on the homepage ↗</a></section></div></Shell>
